00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:25.320
A job in which children's
trust is essential.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.490
Before I go to bed, I'm not confident

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.620
that I can get up okay
the following morning.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.960
We'll start shooting now! Three, two...

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.580
When a bus that goes somewhere other
than my work stops in front of me,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.040
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.040
I sometimes have a strong impulse
to get on it for some reason.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.130
When I try foods that I remember
tasting good in the past,

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.710
I'm Uramichi Oniisan,
your gymnast Oniisan!

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:50.340
I find that now they
don't taste very good.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:53.760
"Together with Maman"

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.100
Easy kanji sometimes slip my mind,
and I can't write them.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.980
I should know me better than anyone in
the world, and yet, I can't trust myself.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:04.690
So, I don't have the capacity
to believe in someone else at all.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.360
It's time for the fun ABC Exercise!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.950
Gather around, kids!

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.660
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.780
Hm? What's the matter?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.870
Is it true that you're good at drawing?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.750
No, it's a lie.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:24.920
Usao-<i>kun </i>told me...
that you can do anything!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.380
Usao-<i>kun </i>told me that!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:38.430
Usao-<i>kun </i>said that you can draw <i>KiraPure</i>!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.350
He said that?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.220
He did.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.020
Kumatani!

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.730
I'm Kumao-<i>kun</i>, kuma.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:46.820
Hey, hey. Draw <i>KiraPure </i>now!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:47.820
What's that?

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.200
It's probably an anime show
for girls airing on Sunday morning.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.410
Saya-<i>chan</i>. To tell you the truth,
I don't know that <i>Kira</i>-something at all.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:58.240
I like KiraPure Pink the best!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.750
Um...

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.750
Draw KiraPure Blue for me!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:04.200
"Twinkling"
"Excited"

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.870
Err...

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.960
Okay.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.590
I'll draw my idea of
that <i>Kira</i>-something--

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:16.760
<i>KiraPure</i>!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.020
Yeah, that. I'll do my best
and draw them, okay?

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:27.650
Even though I can't even trust myself,
kids believe in me so purely like this.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:33.200
As an Oniisan in an educational program,
I'd like to live up to their expectations.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.660
They don't look like that at all!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.040
Creepy!

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:40.610
Scary!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:40.870
What's this?!

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.330
--I'm appalled!
--Absurdly so!

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.960
What're you thinking?!

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.840
"Faith"... "Trust"... No matter how much
time and effort it takes to gain them,

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.880
it only takes a second to lose them.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.970
So, it's not true that
you can do anything...

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:00.180
And, once you lose them,
it's hard to get them back.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.770
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:09.060
Leave the rest to me.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.900
You fought well.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.530
It's Iketeru Oniisan!

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.280
Hello, kids!

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:19.530
You know, the KiraPure that
Uramichi Oniisan drew are very creepy.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.830
You kids are too young
to see that drawing.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:27.080
But I guess that can't be helped
because KiraPure are hard to draw.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.790
I don't have much confidence,
either, but I'll try my best.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.590
Um... I didn't say this earlier,

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:37.130
but my mom also said that
she couldn't draw them well.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.430
Okay. It's done!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.430
How's this?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.310
Amazing!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.520
Wow, that's them!

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.680
It's Pure Pink and Pure Blue!

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.850
Wh-Why can you draw them?!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.860
I did an image search for them earlier.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.230
That's all?!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.320
I like your drawing better than mine.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.990
Please keep drawing, okay?

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.580
Iketeru Oniisan...

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.990
Well, I don't wanna draw
in the first place.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:07.410
This guy's potential is unlimited.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.120
m 840 115 l 852 278 577 245 600 89

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.120
Green Room
for Uramichi 
Omota-sama

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.340
Please hold on a sec!

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.250
Uramichi-<i>san</i>! You got it wrong!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.130
I said it light-heartedly.
It was like a joke.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.970
Uramichi-<i>san</i>! Look this way!

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:17.970
Usahara.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.380
Yes, sir!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.050
Do you believe in God?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.970
Huh? Well...

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.020
I was told that, if I believed in God,

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:29.810
I'd be saved from all anxieties,
worries, and stupid <i>kohai</i>.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.730
What?

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:35.610
But... it's faster if I deal with
those things myself, isn't it?

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.820
What? Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.950
Ow, ow, ow, ow...!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.240
Do you believe in God?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.410
Of course, I do.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.830
I see.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:51.250
Owww!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.000
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.300
Okay!

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:01.800
Okay!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.930
Okay, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>... here!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.220
"Together with Maman"

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.100
Hmm...

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.770
It looks good!

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.190
It does!

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.600
Well then...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.480
Ah...

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.070
Uramichi Oniisan is here.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.900
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.530
Good work!

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.410
Thank you.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.780
I know this is sudden,
but which do you prefer:

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:27.370
going home late tonight or
getting up early tomorrow morning?

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.960
What? I'd say neither.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:32.620
I'm just speaking hypothetically.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:37.670
If it's hypothetically... speaking...

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.670
Yeah.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.050
I'd choose... going home late tonight?

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:45.140
Okay! Come on! Work is fun,
isn't it, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>?!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.060
Where do you wanna go for dinner?

